{# THE BANDED HEAD OF A DEPARTMENT CARD — the mark, the name, the scope, what
   it reads, and the run of figures its modules publish.

   ONE HEAD, THREE SURFACES. The organization's register, an area's Departments
   tab and that area's configure section all draw a department the same way; only
   what is under the head differs. Two heads would be two departments.

   `expandable` is the one switch: a card whose body opens carries the labelled
   disclosure, and a card that is already open — the configure section's — does
   not offer to open it again. #}
{% set uuid = department.uuidString %}
{% set area = department.area %}
{% set filled = people %}
{% set expandable = expandable|default(false) %}
    <div class="dc-hd">
        <span class="ov-mk">{{ mark }}</span>
        <div class="dc-bd">
            <span class="nmrow">
                <a class="ov-nm" href="{{ path('team_department_show', {uuid: uuid}) }}">{{ department.name }}</a>
                <span class="ov-sc{{ area ? ' area' : '' }}">{{ area ? area.name : 'Org-wide' }}</span>
                {% if not department.active %}<span class="chip stoff">inactive</span>{% endif %}
            </span>
            <div class="dc-sub">
                {%- if modules is not empty -%}
                    Reads <b>{{ modules|map(m => m.name)|join('</b>, <b>')|raw }}</b>
                    {{- area ? ' in ' ~ area.name : ' across every area' }}
                {%- else -%}
                    Attaches no module yet &mdash; it shapes emphasis and holds positions
                {%- endif -%}
                &middot; {{ positions|length }} position{{ positions|length == 1 ? '' : 's' }}
                &middot; <b>{{ filled }}</b> {{ filled == 1 ? 'person' : 'people' }}
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dc-act">
            {% if expandable %}
            {# THE DISCLOSURE IS LABELLED AND IT NAMES ITS STATE. A bare
               chevron in the corner said neither what it did nor which way
               it was; this reads EXPAND shut and COLLAPSE open, in the
               action cluster beside Open and at Open's own height.

               A STATE VERB, NEVER A COUNT. "3 positions" on a button says
               what is inside rather than what pressing it does, and it
               changes under the reader when somebody files a position.

               IT IS A LINK, so which card is open stays in the address and
               the label is the server's answer — there is no state in the
               browser to keep in step. #}
            <a class="ovx xdisc" href="{{ open ? here : here ~ ('?' in here ? '&' : '?') ~ 'open=' ~ uuid ~ '#d-' ~ uuid }}"
               aria-expanded="{{ open ? 'true' : 'false' }}"
               aria-label="{{ open ? 'Collapse' : 'Expand' }} {{ department.name }}">
                <span class="t">{{ open ? 'Collapse' : 'Expand' }}</span>{{ ux_icon('shell:chevron-down') }}
            </a>
            {% endif %}
            <a class="ov-open" href="{{ path('team_department_show', {uuid: uuid}) }}" title="Open {{ department.name }}">Open {{ ux_icon('shell:arrow-right') }}</a>
        </div>
        {# WHAT THE ATTACHED MODULES PUBLISH. A department that attaches one
           which publishes nothing for the period says that, in the module's
           name, rather than leaving the run empty. #}
        <div class="dcrun">
            {% for figure in figures %}
                <span class="f"><b>{{ figure.display }}</b>{{ figure.unit }} {{ figure.label|lower }}</span>
            {% else %}
                <span class="f q">{{ modules is empty ? 'No module attached — no figure' : 'The attached modules publish no figure for this period' }}</span>
            {% endfor %}
            {# GOALS ARE DEFERRED, and the card says so in the house's words
               rather than drawing an empty dot rail.

               WHEN THEY ARRIVE THE RAIL HAS FOUR STATES, not three — the
               design settled them on 2026-09-19: met, at risk and missed as
               filled dots; NO GOAL DECLARED as a DASHED hollow ring; and NO
               FIGURE YET as a SOLID hollow ring (`.gdots i.nofig`). The last
               two read alike at a glance and mean opposite things — nobody
               set a target, versus nobody has reported one — so the goals
               port ships all four or it ships a rail that lies. #}
            <span class="gl"><span class="gn">Goals not kept yet</span></span>
        </div>
    </div>

